   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th salivary gland carcinomas & AJCC 9th staging",
    "intro": "Report histologic subtype, grade/high-grade transformation, capsular invasion depth for carcinoma ex pleomorphic adenoma (intracapsular = pTis; minimally invasive <= 4–6 mm vs widely invasive), and AJCC 9th pN (pN1 = 1–3 nodes without ENE; pN2 = > 3 nodes or any definitive ENE).",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Carcinoma ex pleomorphic adenoma (Ca ex PA)",
      "points": [
       "Malignant epithelial neoplasm (most commonly salivary duct carcinoma, adenocarcinoma NOS, or myoepithelial carcinoma) arising within a pre-existing or residual hyalinised/chondromyxoid pleomorphic adenoma (PLAG1 or HMGA2 rearranged).",
       "Intracapsular (non-invasive) Ca ex PA is staged as pTis; measure maximum distance of invasion beyond the PA capsule for minimally invasive vs widely invasive disease."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Carcinoma Ex Pleomorphic Adenoma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
