        "credit": "Nephron",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carcinoma_ex_pleomorphic_adenoma_--_intermed_mag.jpg"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Molecularly defined WHO 5th salivary gland carcinomas",
      "points": [
       "Mucoepidermoid carcinoma: CRTC1/CRTC3::MAML2 fusion; grade using AFIP/Brandwein/MSKCC criteria (cystic component, PNI, necrosis, mitoses, anaplasia).",
       "Adenoid cystic carcinoma: MYB/MYBL1::NFIB fusion; record % solid growth (> 30% solid = high-grade behaviour) and perineural invasion.",
       "Acinic cell carcinoma: NR4A3 nuclear overexpression; Secretory carcinoma: ETV6::NTRK3 (S100+/mammaglobin+/DOG1-); Hyalinising clear cell carcinoma: EWSR1::ATF1; Microsecretory adenocarcinoma: MEF2C::SS18.",
       "Salivary duct carcinoma: apocrine comedonecrosis morphology; test AR (strongly positive) and HER2 (IHC/ISH) for targeted therapy."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Salivary Gland Carcinomas",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ]
     }
